    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0061" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v23p2/pg33"/>

                <head>17. Telegram From the Embassy in Korea to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d17-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-02-07T23:00:00+08:30"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                                1955—11 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>877. Tokyo pass CINCUNC, CG AFFE/Army Eight and CAG. DA 975505<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d17-f2"/> discussed this morning Tokyo. As indicated Embtel 851 rptd
                    Tokyo 580,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d17-f3"/> I envisage harassing delays in
                    procedure outlined para three which may be exploited by Communists and I saw
                    little prospect of MAC action favorable to US. The considerable present risk of
                    explosive situation in ROK (Ref CINCUNC 71216 for JCS Jan 24)<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d17-f4"/> may be aggravated by delays. Therefore unless Dept able
                    obtain effective withdrawal commitment from Swiss and Swedes UNC should be
                    prepared act along lines para four whenever local situation demands.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Briggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 795.00/2–755. Top Secret; Priority.
                    Repeated to Tokyo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="2" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d14">Document 14</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f3" n="3" xml:id="d17-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram 851 from Seoul, February 1, the Embassy called attention to CINCUNC
                    telegram C–71309, January 31 (see <ref target="#d10-f3">footnote 3, Document
                        10</ref>). The Embassy agreed that it might prove necessary in the last
                    analysis to declare paragraphs 13c and 13d of the Armistice Agreement invalid,
                    but the first step should be to formulate a U.S. reply to the Swiss and
                    Swedes.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f4" n="4" xml:id="d17-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d14-f2">footnote 2, Document 14</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
